      "side": 1,
      "message": "Bit confusing that manual ended up above nightly for 2025.04.12, even though nighly is labeled \"latest\". I thought GitHub would sort by semver order, in which `v2025.04.12-03.06.48` is a prerelease that I\u0027m pretty sure should come before the corresponding full release `v2025.04.12`. But I think it\u0027s actually sorting alphanumerically.\nhttps://github.com/kainino0x/dawn/releases\n\nMaybe we should just take the commit time of the commit we\u0027re building and use that as the version, no nightly vs manual distinction. Maybe include the user+branch name if it\u0027s not `google/main`?\n\nMaybe we should just produce a version number based on how far we are from the initial commit (`git rev-list --count f07e3bd4c9553e7cd2af058fb6b8482721e4e486..HEAD`), especially if we only do this on `google/main` which we can mostly assume will move monotonically forward?",
